.Dd August 7, 2026
.Dt JEEP-LIST 1
.Os Jeep DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm jeep-list
.Nd list system information
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl J No \&|
.Fl "-no-jpm"
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists system information,
including the bundles installed in the current
.Sy syspath .
By default,
.Nm
will list both Janet bundles and JPM bundles.
The
.Fl "-no-jpm"
option can be used to exclude JPM bundles from the results.
.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Fl J No \&|
.Fl "-no-jpm"
.Xc
Exclude JPM bundles from the listing.
.El
.Pp
For more information about
.Sy JPM bundles ,
.Sy Janet bundles
and the
.Sy syspath ,
see CONCEPTS in
.Xr jeep 1 .
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To list system information,
including all installed bundles:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep list
.Ed
.Pp
To list system information,
showing installed Janet bundles only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep list -J
.Ed
.
